  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math>&nbsp;be any two numbers satisfying <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>.</mi></math> Then, the foot of perpendicular from the origin on the variable line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> lies on :",
    "image": null
  },
